& [NecessaryCorrection]
  + the model should not author the complete lifecycle request because it is proof-bearing host data rather than generative semantic output
  + the experiment host should deterministically construct or load and directly register one admitted fixture before inference
  + the model-visible task should receive the returned handle and decide or reproduce only the closed VALIDATE command

& [MissingBridge]
  + llama_tool_reflection currently calls an in-process hard-coded reflect function and is not an MCP client
  + add a bounded host bridge from one validated OpenAI-style function call to the Slice10 stdio MCP process
  + preserve assistant tool_calls append the structured tool result with the matching tool_call_id and issue a second inference request with tool_choice none
  + import a deliberately small projection of lifecycle outcome stage disposition and source identity rather than asking the model to echo the complete response

& [FixtureDependency]
  + the current complete lifecycle generator is a Rust integration-test fixture and is not a separately versioned experiment input artifact
  + before live measurement preserve and SJS-process either a deterministic public fixture generator or one checked-in sanitized lifecycle request with digest lineage
  + never ask the model to invent signatures trust context artifact receipts or verification facts

& [MeasurementArms]
  + [A_stateless] repeat the complete Slice8 request for each validation call
  + [B_volatile_custody] host registers once then repeats only Slice10 compact handle validation
  + compare exact core response equality prompt tokens completion tokens serialized request bytes first-call latency repeated-call latency tool-call validity and second-checkpoint import validity
  + include at least one lifecycle-valid and one retained-lifecycle-refused request
  + include process restart as an expected visible refusal and exclude restart trials from steady-state latency averages

& [AcceptanceShape]
  + equal semantic responses across A and B
  + byte and token savings reported separately so transport compression is not mislabeled as model-context compression
  + no provider-private reasoning retained
  + no llama.cpp modification provider installation remote machine or durable custody needed

& [RecommendedNextSource]
  + preserve a bounded Slice11 live tool-loop measurement source selecting local host endpoint model fixture identities trial count timeout evidence sanitation and no-effect boundaries
